 How easy is it to switch to the default theme if I want to choose option 2?

  Searched for 2 patterns, ran 1 shell command

Mechanically trivial, but there's a hidden cost. Two mechanical changes:

1. zk.xml:49 — change <value>sapphire</value> to <value>breeze</value> (or just delete the library-property block, since breeze is ZK's built-in default).
2. Delete WEB-INF/lib/sapphire.jar (no longer referenced by anything once the property changes).

I checked for other places tied to "sapphire" specifically — there's only one, a CSS override at libreplan_zk.css:2304-2306 that forces a white background on the timetracker grid header "because native background is looked very awful" in sapphire. That's harmless either way (won't break breeze).

The real cost isn't the config change — it's that libreplan_zk.css is 2300+ lines of custom overrides layered on top of whichever base theme is active. Those overrides (colors, borders, spacing, box-shadows) were very likely eyeballed and tuned against sapphire's look. Breeze has a different default palette/chrome, so switching themes is effectively a full re-skin: every screen needs a visual pass to catch clashes — colors that no longer match, spacing assumptions that broke, etc. There's no way to know the scope without actually running the app in each theme and comparing screens.

So: config change is a 5-minute edit; the "is it actually done" bar depends on how much visual regression you're willing to accept across the whole app.

