Short answer: for the free/CE path, not really — Breeze is the only actively-maintained, open-source theme bundled with ZK. Everything else has been consolidated into a paid product.

What I found:

- Breeze — the built-in CE default, LGPL-licensed, actively maintained, ships with ZK core.
- Sapphire, Silvertail, Atlantic — used to be available as separate lightweight theme jars (there's actually a real org.zkoss.theme:sapphire Maven artifact, last released Feb 2024, up to ZK ~9.6). But as of ZK 10.0.0, all three are deprecated in favor of the commercial ZK Theme Pack (26 themes, requires a PE/EE license, distributed via ZK's premium downloads or EE Maven repo) — Breeze itself is also deprecated in ZK 10 with a recommendation to move to a Theme Pack theme.

Practical implication for LibrePlan: your vendored sapphire.jar is a hand-me-down from 2017 (ZK ~8.0 era) that's already missing newer widget CSS. There is an officially published org.zkoss.theme:sapphire artifact that's newer and would likely include checkbox.css.dsp/rating.css.dsp — pulling that as a real Maven dependency (if it's accessible without an EE license — worth checking, since ZK's own repo may gate it) would be a cleaner fix than hand-patching the old jar. But since Sapphire itself is now deprecated upstream, that's a dead end long-term: the sustainable free option is Breeze.

